wasm-ld: no runtime relocation for R_WASM_MEMORY_ADDR_LOCREL_I32 in PIC data.

A location-relative relocation (Swift's relative pointers: conformance
records, type descriptors, mangled names' symbolic references) between two
places in one module holds wherever the module is loaded, and `relocate`
writes its value at link time. In a shared library (`--experimental-pic
-shared`) wasm-ld also emitted a runtime relocation for it in
__wasm_apply_data_relocs, adding __memory_base to the relative value (or
storing the symbol's GOT address, for an exported symbol): a Swift side
module's conformance records then point outside memory and the runtime's
first conformance scan traps. Upstream LLVM rejects the relocation instead
("invalid runtime relocation type in data section"), so a Swift side module
doesn't link there either; the same change belongs upstream (with
R_WASM_MEMORY_ADDR_LOCREL_I64, which this LLVM lacks).

Against swiftlang/llvm-project swift-6.4.2-RELEASE (fb5f84d9). With it, lld's
wasm tests pass (213; shared-locrel.s, new here, fails without it), and the
examples' Storybook linked as a side module renders byte for byte as its
self-contained reactor does (WasmDynamicLinker, //shared/wasm_host).

The same commit: pawlowskialex/llvm-project, branch wasm-ld-pic-locrel-6.4.2
(0ecbfee3). Not applied by any build here yet: the toolchain's wasm-ld comes
from swift.org's release (docs/side_modules.md).

diff --git a/lld/test/wasm/shared-locrel.s b/lld/test/wasm/shared-locrel.s
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..3502334d6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lld/test/wasm/shared-locrel.s
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# Location-relative data relocations (R_WASM_MEMORY_ADDR_LOCREL_I32, which
+# Swift emits for its relative pointers) are position-independent: in a shared
+# library their link-time value holds wherever the library is loaded, so no
+# runtime relocation may be generated for them, whether the target is hidden
+# or exported. An absolute address (R_WASM_MEMORY_ADDR_I32) still gets one.
+
+# RUN: llvm-mc -filetype=obj -triple=wasm32-unknown-unknown -o %t.o %s
+# RUN: wasm-ld --experimental-pic -shared -o %t.wasm %t.o
+# RUN: obj2yaml %t.wasm | FileCheck %s
+# RUN: llvm-objdump --disassemble-symbols=__wasm_apply_data_relocs --no-show-raw-insn --no-leading-addr %t.wasm | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes DIS
+
+.globaltype __memory_base, i32, immutable
+
+.section .data.hidden_target,"",@
+.globl hidden_target
+.hidden hidden_target
+.p2align 2
+hidden_target:
+  .int32 1
+  .size hidden_target, 4
+
+.section .data.exported_target,"",@
+.globl exported_target
+.p2align 2
+exported_target:
+  .int32 2
+  .size exported_target, 4
+
+.section .data.pointers,"",@
+.globl pointers
+.p2align 2
+pointers:
+  .int32 hidden_target - pointers
+  .int32 exported_target - (pointers + 4)
+  .int32 hidden_target
+  .size pointers, 12
+
+# hidden_target at 0, exported_target at 4, pointers at 8: the relative
+# pointers are 0 - 8 and 4 - 12, written at link time; the absolute one is 0
+# until __wasm_apply_data_relocs adds __memory_base.
+# CHECK:        - Type:            DATA
+# CHECK:            Content:         0100000002000000F8FFFFFFF8FFFFFF00000000
+
+# Only the absolute pointer, at 16, is relocated at load.
+# DIS:      <__wasm_apply_data_relocs>:
+# DIS-EMPTY:
+# DIS-NEXT:   i32.const 16
+# DIS-NEXT:   global.get 0
+# DIS-NEXT:   i32.add
+# DIS-NEXT:   global.get 0
+# DIS-NEXT:   i32.const 0
+# DIS-NEXT:   i32.add
+# DIS-NEXT:   i32.store 0
+# DIS-NEXT:   end
diff --git a/lld/wasm/InputChunks.cpp b/lld/wasm/InputChunks.cpp
index 181221a77..e74b19a83 100644
--- a/lld/wasm/InputChunks.cpp
+++ b/lld/wasm/InputChunks.cpp
@@ -433,6 +433,18 @@ bool InputChunk::generateRelocationCode(raw_ostream &os) const {
     if (!requiresRuntimeReloc)
       continue;
 
+    // A location-relative relocation (Swift's relative pointers) between two
+    // places in this module holds wherever the module is loaded: `relocate`
+    // already wrote its value. Adding __memory_base to it (or storing the
+    // symbol's GOT address, for one the module exports) would break it.
+    if (rel.Type == R_WASM_MEMORY_ADDR_LOCREL_I32) {
+      if (!sym->isDefined())
+        error(toString(file) + ": relocation " + relocTypeToString(rel.Type) +
+              " cannot be used against an undefined symbol `" +
+              toString(*sym) + "`");
+      continue;
+    }
+
     LLVM_DEBUG(dbgs() << "gen reloc: type=" << relocTypeToString(rel.Type)
                       << " addend=" << rel.Addend << " index=" << rel.Index
                       << " output offset=" << offset << "\n");
